Cudy TR3600 v1: stop the fan running at 50 % from 40 C upwards

mt7987.dtsi maps the 40 C active-low trip to fan level 1, so the fan runs
at 50 % whenever the SoC is above 40 C - which is always.  A unit sitting
idle at 57 C therefore keeps the fan audible with nothing to do.

The vendor DTS maps that same trip to fan level 0 (fan off) and only
starts the fan at 85 C.  Keep the fan off while the SoC is cool, but use a
gentler four-step ramp than the vendor table:

  < 60 C : off
  65 C   : level 1 (PWM 64,  25 %)
  75 C   : level 2 (PWM 160, 63 %)
  85 C   : level 3 (PWM 255, 100 %)

cooling-levels stays at four states because the tr3600-fan daemon and its
LuCI page only accept levels 0-3.

Verified by compiling the DTS: active-low/med/high resolve to 65000/75000/
85000 with 5000 hysteresis, the existing cooling-maps are kept and no
duplicate trips are created.

Signed-off-by: TR3600 build kit <noreply@example.com>
---
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@
 &fan {
 	fan-supply = <&fan_3p3v>;
 	pwms = <&pwm 0 50000 0>;
+	cooling-levels = <0 64 160 255>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -280,3 +281,32 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart0_pins>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * mt7987.dtsi maps the 40 C trip to fan level 1, which leaves the fan
+ * spinning at 50 % from 40 C upwards - clearly audible at idle (the unit
+ * sits around 57 C doing nothing).  Move the first step up to 65 C and use
+ * a gentler ramp.  The vendor DTS keeps the fan off below 85 C; 65 C keeps
+ * a usable margin without the constant noise.
+ *
+ * cooling-levels stays at four states (0..3) because the tr3600-fan daemon
+ * and its LuCI page only accept levels 0-3.
+ */
+&cpu_thermal {
+	trips {
+		cpu_trip_active_low: active-low {
+			temperature = <65000>;
+			hysteresis = <5000>;
+		};
+
+		cpu_trip_active_med: active-med {
+			temperature = <75000>;
+			hysteresis = <5000>;
+		};
+
+		cpu_trip_active_high: active-high {
+			temperature = <85000>;
+			hysteresis = <5000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
